 Linux Commands Every Engineer Should Know (One-Liners & Quick Hacks)

Why type 10 commands when 1 works?

These powerful one-liners let engineers fix, debug, and automate on the fly 👇

📌 Kill all processes of a program
pkill -f program_name

📌 Check top memory consumers
ps aux --sort=-%mem | head -10

📌 Find & delete old log files
find /var/log -type f -mtime +30 -exec rm -f {} \;

📌 Quick disk usage by folder
du -sh * | sort -h

📌 Monitor log in real-time with filtering
tail -f /var/log/syslog | grep error

📌 One-liner network check
ping -c 3 google.com && echo "Online" || echo "Offline"

📌 Backup a directory with timestamp
tar -czvf backup_$(date +%F).tar.gz /path/to/dir

📌 Count files by type
find . -type f | wc -l

💡 These one-liners = instant troubleshooting, automation, and DevOps efficiency.

Linux mastery is about thinking in one-liners. 🐧
